venv/
.venv/
# `B1587`. A pattern with no `/` before its wildcard matches at the top level
# only — Docker's `*` does not cross a `/` (`B447`'s harness measured it:
# 382 untracked `__pycache__/*.pyc` files from a checkout went into the build
# context under the old `__pycache__/` line). These are caches and outputs at
# any depth, so they say so with `**/`.
**/node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/*.egg-info/
# ...but these two stay top-level on purpose: they are the Python packaging
# outputs, and `**/build/` would drop `static/js/editor/build/`, six tracked
# modules the editor imports.
/dist/
/build/
.env
.env.bak.*
# Secrets: keep plaintext and every transient secrets.env variant out of
# the build context. If an encrypted secrets.env is used, it is mounted
# at runtime — never baked into the image. Mirrored in .gitignore.
secrets.env
secrets.env.*
secrets.env~
.secrets.env.swp
.secrets.env.swo
**/#secrets.env#
!secrets.env.example
/data/
/logs/
.git/
.claude/
.playwright-mcp/
.pytest_cache/
.vscode/
.idea/
dev-docs/
docs/
*.md
# ...but the attribution files must ship. NOTICE designates CREDITS.md as the
# third-party notice for this distribution, so `*.md` silently dropping it means
# the image redistributes MIT/BSD/OFL code with no notice attached.
!CREDITS.md
!NOTICE
!LICENSE
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
/reports/
/research_data/
tasks/
_scratch/
compound.config.json
search_analytics.json
**/search_analytics.json
tests/
api/
**/*.log
chart.png
timetree*.png
*_signin_page.png
*_calendar_view.png
.gitignore
